Assessment;
Hello! Looking at your maize crop, my image assessment suggests it might be dealing with maize common rust. Please remember that this image result is just an initial look and should always be confirmed right there in your field before you make any big decisions, especially before applying any chemical treatments. Also, I must let you know that we do not have specific local field evidence on hand for this disease, so getting a local opinion is very important.

What You Should Do Now;
If you are wondering whether you can use double the dose or mix two chemicals to stop the disease from spreading fast, please do not do that. You should only use the exact chemical treatment listed in our verified guidelines, spray evenly, and never increase the label rate. Using extra or mixing unverified products can harm your crop, waste your money, and create other problems. Instead, inspect your fields closely to confirm the rust is actually there, and consider reaching out to a local extension officer to get expert eyes on your plants.

How to Manage and Prevent Further Spread;
To keep the disease under control, you should only apply a treatment if the rust is truly confirmed in your field. When you do spray, make sure you cover the plants evenly. Keep a close eye on your crop so you can catch any changes early, and always follow the safety guidelines carefully to protect yourself and your harvest.

Verified Treatment;
Because we have a verified rule for managing this situation, here is the exact treatment you should follow if you decide to spray:
* **Chemical:** Azoxystrobin 18.2% + Cyproconazole 7.3% SC
* **Dose:** 1 ml/L using 500 L water/ha (500 liters of water per hectare)
* **Timing:** Apply either preventively or right at the first appearance of the disease. If needed, you can repeat the application after 10-15 days.
* **Maximum Applications:** You can apply this a maximum of 2 per season.
* **PHI (Pre-Harvest Interval):** The PHI is 52 days, which means you must wait at least 52 days after your last spray before you harvest your maize.
* **Re-entry Period:** The re-entry period is 24 hours, meaning nobody should go back into the treated field without proper protection until at least 24 hours have passed.
* **IPM Note:** Use this chemical only if the rust is confirmed. Spray evenly and do not increase the label rate.

Safety and Field Confirmation;
Before spraying, please double-check your fields in person to make sure the disease is actually there. When working with the chemical, always follow the re-entry period of 24 hours to keep everyone safe, and respect the 52-day waiting period before harvest. If you are ever unsure about anything or need extra help, please contact a local extension officer.

Sources;
* [Syngenta India Limited Safety Rule Source URL](https://ppqs.gov.in/sites/default/files/azoxystrobin_18.2_cyproconazole_7.3_sc93fsyngenta_india_limited_1-merged.pdf)
